Difficulty, Fellowship and Travel windows, plus this session's fixes

Three whole features had never been committed anywhere -- core_difficulty,
core_fellowship and core_travel were untracked, so the only copy was in the dev
container. That is the same exposure CLAUDE.md section 0 records for the Lua in
2026-07.

New translation units, each its own module with no detours of its own, calling
in through the dsp_chat / InterpretCmd / ProcessGameEvents hooks this dll
already owns:

  core_difficulty  the /pick window for Normal / Nightmare / Hell / Inferno
  core_fellowship  the fellowship roster, invites and campfires
  core_travel      the region travel window

Fixes in this session's modified files:

  core_travel      WriteChatColor is a GUARANTEED crash in this dll -- with
                   isMQInjectsEnabled false the chat hook is never installed, so
                   the trampoline keeps its DETOUR_TRAMPOLINE_EMPTY body, which
                   is a deliberate null dereference. Pressing Travel with nothing
                   selected took the client down every time. Now sets the
                   ATW_Hint label the XML already shipped.
  core_fellowship  the echo matcher keyed on "says, '" which does not match
                   "You say, '" -- so it swallowed the command on everyone
                   ELSE's screen and left it on the presser's, the wrong way
                   round. Now tests both whole strings.
  core_bazaar.h    /shield was the only rewritten command with no entry in the
                   echo list, so it announced itself to everyone in earshot.
  core_aotmenu     the launcher re-expanded on every zone. Now loads and stores
                   its ini state so a closed or minimised menu stays that way.
  EQClasses.cpp    FUNCTION_AT_ADDRESS thunks for CSidlScreenWnd LoadIniInfo and
                   StoreIniInfo -- declared and offset-mapped but never bound,
                   which only surfaced as an unresolved external at link time.

